{#- 01 Old Town — white ground. The anchor stays #oldtown: it is what the
    homepage cards and every link from before this page was renamed use. -#}
<section class="n-bg-white" id="oldtown" aria-labelledby="e1-h">
<div class="n-wrap" style="padding-block:clamp(28px,3.5vw,60px)">
<div class="n-entry">
<span class="n-num" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:clamp(2rem,1.5rem + 1.6vw,3.25rem)">01</span>
<div>
<h2 class="n-h2" id="e1-h" style="font-size:clamp(1.75rem,1.4rem + 1.4vw,2.75rem);color:var(--n-evergreen)">Walk Old Town</h2>
<p class="n-body" style="margin:16px 0 0;max-width:58ch">The brick and false-front commercial block on Second Avenue is the reason the rest of this page exists. It dates from the railroad period and it is still where the community gathers.</p>
<p class="n-body" style="margin:14px 0 0;max-width:58ch;font-size:.9375rem">Walk it end to end in about ten minutes. Cross streets are short and the sidewalks are continuous.</p>
<dl style="margin:22px 0 0">
<div class="n-fact">
<dt class="n-label n-label--quiet">Getting there</dt>
<dd class="n-body" style="margin:0;font-size:.9375rem">Street parking along Second Avenue and the adjacent lots.</dd>
</div>
<div class="n-fact">
<dt class="n-label n-label--quiet">Best for</dt>
<dd class="n-body" style="margin:0;font-size:.9375rem">Coffee, browsing, and the historic building fronts.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<div class="n-btns" style="margin-top:20px">
<a class="n-btn n-btn--ghost" href="/old-town-niwot/">The Old Town guide</a>
</div>
</div>
