{#- 05 Whistle Stop Park and the trails — white ground. The anchor stays
    #outdoors for the same reason #oldtown does. -#}
<section class="n-bg-white" id="outdoors" aria-labelledby="e5-h">
<div class="n-wrap" style="padding-block:clamp(28px,3.5vw,60px)">
<div class="n-entry">
<span class="n-num" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:clamp(2rem,1.5rem + 1.6vw,3.25rem)">05</span>
<div>
<h2 class="n-h2" id="e5-h" style="font-size:clamp(1.75rem,1.4rem + 1.4vw,2.75rem);color:var(--n-evergreen)">The park, and the trail out of town</h2>
<p class="n-body" style="margin:16px 0 0;max-width:58ch">Whistle Stop Park sits at the south-west corner of Murray Street and First Avenue, at the edge of Old Town, and keeps the restored caboose. The Longmont-to-Boulder (LoBo) Regional Trail &#8212; twelve miles between the two cities through Gunbarrel and Niwot &#8212; runs through the community and joins the local trail network, and Left Hand Creek crosses the fields east of the built-up blocks.</p>
<p class="n-body" style="margin:14px 0 0;max-width:58ch;font-size:.9375rem">Trail surfaces, closures and dog rules are set by Boulder County Parks &amp; Open Space rather than by a town, since Niwot is unincorporated. The parks and trails page collects the county&#8217;s maps and rules in one place.</p>
<dl style="margin:22px 0 0">
<div class="n-fact">
<dt class="n-label n-label--quiet">The trail</dt>
<dd class="n-body" style="margin:0;font-size:.9375rem"><a class="n-link" href="https://bouldercounty.gov/open-space/parks-and-trails/lobo-trail/" rel="noopener">LoBo Regional Trail, Boulder County <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></dd>
</div>
<div class="n-fact">
<dt class="n-label n-label--quiet">Best for</dt>
<dd class="n-body" style="margin:0;font-size:.9375rem">Walking and cycling; the eastern fields at sunset.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<div class="n-btns" style="margin-top:20px">
<a class="n-btn n-btn--ghost" href="/parks-trails/">Parks &amp; trails</a>
</div>
</div>
<figure class="n-ph-lg" style="margin:0">
{% photo "front-range-sunset-trail.jpg", "Sunset over the Front Range from a dirt trail on the grassland edge of Niwot", "(max-width: 900px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width: 1440px) 38vw, 525px", "display:block;width:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 58%" %}
